post.description:
Accepts an Idempotency-Key header. The member joins the business as staff and gets its dashboard (BIZ-03). 409 business_exists when
the member owns or works for a business already; 404 business_unavailable when the business is gone or a block came between;
409 limit_reached when the team is full. The member's other invitations end.

Accepts an Idempotency-Key header. Founder and admins, in every join mode. The member hears about it in the app and accepts with
POST me/crew-invites/{invite}/accept. Unknown, not visible, blocked either way, already a member or invited: 422 on `username`;
at most 50 open invitations (409 limit_reached).

get.description:
Guests too (the data of WEB-09 /e/{slug}). The exact place only for the organiser and going members of an after_rsvp event;
everybody else reads `location.exact` false with the city and the area point. A draft, pending or rejected event is the
organiser's alone; for everybody else, as for a missing one: 404 event_unavailable.

post.description:
Multipart. Accepts an Idempotency-Key header. Up to 15 MB, JPEG, PNG or WebP by content (413, 415);
HEIC is converted by the client first. Status is `processing` when the server retries in the background.
M5.9a: `plate_blur` + `blur_regions` pixelate number plates before any file is written (ADR-509).

`attempt_id` from the `link_required` answer and the 6-digit code mailed to the existing account. Links the provider, mails the
owner, and signs in (with two-factor on: the challenge, as at sign-in). Wrong code: 422 `invalid_code` with `attempts_left`;
expired: 422 `code_expired`; locked: 429 `email_code_locked`. A provider ID already linked elsewhere: 409 `provider_already_linked`.

gallery.description:
M5.6 post-event gallery (flag events.gallery; absent while it is off). `open`: uploads are accepted now; `closes_at` = end
(or start + 6 h) + 14 days; `count` approved photos; `pending` the organiser's queue (null for everybody else);
`mine_pending` the reader's own photos waiting (null for guests); `preview` up to six approved, newest approval first.
